      "writtenOn": "2018-06-04T12:16:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t do this due to the cascade of conditions. If I moved this condition at 6960, I could end up deciding to skip an idle CPU that\u0027s in a deeper idle state without checking if this CPU is better from the point of view of it\u0027s capacity_orig. I would always want to choose a bigger CPU even if it\u0027s in a deeper idle state for the boosted case and a smaller CPU, even if it\u0027s in a deeper idle state for the non-boosted case.\nSo we have to choose capacity over the depth of the idle state, so conditions applied to capacity_orig should come first.\n\nI could move up both conditions, especially given the patch at https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/673169/6 which makes things easier. The only question mark would remain around the prefer_idle case when you only have active CPUs. At the moment it does not filter based on capacity_orig, it just looks for the highest spare, independent of the task being boosted or not, so we\u0027d no longer be functionally equivalent. This would be a different patch, that I\u0027m reluctant to introduce as I\u0027d prefer not to tinker with find_best_target much more given plans to remove parts of it or entirely.",
